lasso-mode
==========

lasso-mode is a derivative and aggregate work built on four MIT-licensed
open-source projects. Each is used under the terms of the MIT License.

1. pstack
   Author:  Lauren Tan (poteto)
   Source:  https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
   Commit:  e46364b8be46000b7df0f260550cd712afbb8d36
   Use:     The workflow engine. The router skill (lasso-mode), the 20
            principle skills, the 16 playbooks, and the workflow skills
            (how, why, architect, arena, interrogate, tdd, reflect, unslop,
            recall, blast-radius, figure-it-out, show-me-your-work,
            automate-me, typescript-best-practices, setup-lasso) are ported
            and adapted from pstack's poteto-mode. Cursor-specific details
            were adapted for Claude Code, and the cross-vendor multi-model
            review panels were reworked into single-provider, divergent-lens
            panels.

2. langchain-skills
   Author:  LangChain
   Source:  https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-skills
   Commit:  c88193a48f387560697e1152e32dc5fd239c83e4
   Use:     Vendored verbatim into skills/stack/ (langchain-fundamentals,
            langchain-middleware, langchain-rag, langchain-dependencies,
            ecosystem-primer, langgraph-fundamentals, langgraph-persistence,
            langgraph-human-in-the-loop, langgraph-cli, deep-agents-core,
            deep-agents-memory, deep-agents-orchestration, managed-deep-agents,
            swarm).

3. agent-skills (Vercel Labs)
   Author:  Vercel
   Source:  https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills
   Commit:  f8a72b9603728bb92a217a879b7e62e43ad76c81
   Use:     Vendored verbatim into skills/stack/vercel-react-best-practices/
            (the react-best-practices skill: React and Next.js performance
            guidelines).

4. skills (David Ondrej)
   Author:  David Ondrej
   Source:  https://github.com/davidondrej/skills
   Commit:  55bb353e9e25464e3f627ec8c48ece2ae83af559
   Use:     Three adaptations. hooks/dangerous-patterns.txt is the denylist
            from his dangerous-patterns.txt, taken close to verbatim with a
            lasso-specific header. hooks/lasso-guard.sh is a rewrite of his
            deny-dangerous.sh, keeping the multi-host payload handling and the
            fail-open posture, adding install/check/test modes and symlink
            resolution. hooks/test-guard.sh is his test harness, retargeted and
            extended with a symlink regression test. skills/goal/ and
            skills/git-worktree/ are rewritten from his goal-loop and
            git-worktree skills: the contract shape, the reward-hacking
            warning, and the worktree bootstrap checklist are his; the prose,
            the principle cross-references, and the /loop-versus-/goal
            distinction are lasso's.

